-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Robison</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name><name><surname>Smithee</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Jarvis</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A prolonged outbreak of Pseudomonas aeruginosa in a neonatal intensive care unit: did staff fingernails play a role in disease transmission?</article-title><source>Infect Control Hosp Epidemiol</source><year>2000</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>80</fpage><lpage>85</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10697282</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1086/501739</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bert</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Maubec</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruneau</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Berry</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Lambert-Zechovsky</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Multi-resistant Pseudomonas aeruginosa outbreak associated with contaminated tap water in a neurosurgery intensive care unit</article-title><source>J Hosp Infect</source><year>1998</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>53</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9617685</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0195-6701(98)90243-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grigis</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Goglio</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Parea</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gnecchi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Minetti</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Barbui</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nosocomial outbre